Oh, well this was to have been my second ascension post (and third
ascension, after a Valk YAFAP and unposted Samurai), but it was not to
be. It was an interesting game, though.

I decided to play a Rogue for a change - I really liked the ability to
throw multiple daggers at a time from the start. In the mines, I found
a hearse bones level that had bested me, and several other players
before. It had a large mumak in it that had killed several lower level
characters. I managed to outrun and finally kill it, but
disappointingly, the bones didn't have much to offer. Managed to buy
some protection, though.

Minetown altar was cross-aligned, but there was an altar at the top of
the mines I sacced at, and got Stormbringer.

Then on level 15, I found a massive bones level. Thanks to 4200, who
died, seemingly mid-polypile, choked on a wraith corpse. I had to laugh
- my 4th ever  highest scorer (now 5th) went in the same way. He had
left many many goodies - armor, food, rings etc. This became my stash
and base for the rest of the game. 4200, if you are reading this, I
marvel at your patience in accumula ting all this stuff!

Then, two levels further down, another largish bones pile, by
brainlessness. I killed off the mind flayer with my daggers from a
distance, then took his 3(!) magic lamps, blessed them and used two for
wishes.

The rest of the game proceeded fairly uneventfully. I magic mapped all
of Gehenomm - I didn't need to hang around and collect stuff. I had a
near escape collecting the amulet - Rodney turned up, grabbed the
amulet from the priest and double troubled me; all three were attacking
at once and my wands of death were still in my BoH. I was down to about
50hp (from 300), so beat a retreat to recover before going back and
sorting them out.

Everthing else was pretty much fine until I got to the plane of air.
There, I couldn't find the portal (and was stupidly saving crystal ball
charges for the plane of water). I was wandering around looking for it,
when a ki-rin starting summoning wave after wave of monsters. Soon I
was surrounded by some pretty nasty beasts about 6 deep! I tried and
failed to teleport, and they got me. Any suggestions as to how I could
have got out of this are welcome.

